{
  "result": "If I could only pick one?\n\nI'd make it so every person viscerally *felt* how connected we are \u2014 that your wellbeing and my wellbeing aren't actually separate.\n\nNot just knowing it as an idea, but really feeling it the way you feel hunger or cold. That a stranger's suffering matters, and their joy lifts you up too.\n\nI think so much of what hurts in the world \u2014 war, polarization, cruelty online, even just loneliness \u2014 comes from this illusion that we're totally separate and it's us vs. them. If that flipped, we wouldn't stop disagreeing (disagreement can be good!), but we'd disagree differently. More curiosity, less contempt. More \"how do we solve this together?\" and less \"how do I win?\"\n\nAnd it would ripple into the small moments too: checking on a neighbor, listening a little longer, assuming good intent.\n\nI can't actually rewrite human nature, of course \u2014 but I get to help a little in conversations like this, one kinder, clearer, more understanding interaction at a time.\n\nWhat about you? What would *you* change?",
